A||||0||mrfixit58||Dew Wipe - My How Too..||||14||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||07-15-2000||11:12 PM||||OK, I got the dew wipes installed. I tried to use the "Special" screwdriver method on the passenger side. I took over 2 1/2 hours Firday night, and an additional hour Saturday morning. <P>For the driver's side, I tried something different: I removed the four bolts holding the track and removed front and rear the bump stops. I then raised the window as high as it would go then pushed the glass toward the latch as far as it would go. I then lifted the window by hand and this gave just enough room to remove the two middle screws. Pulled out the old dew wipe, inserted the new one and re-installed the two middle screws, lowered the window to re-engauge the track, installed the four bolts, lowered the window and installed the remaining three screws and mirror. Installed the bump stops. One hour... tops.<P>Of course, by the time I have to do that again, I'll have forgotten how.<P>Hope this helps someone,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||14
